{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"An ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSTextField","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" label's alignment rect is its text width. The padding its cell draws (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"alignmentRectInsets","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" 2 pt left and right) falls outside it. So ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"SidebarCellView.contentWidth(...)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" — symbol column + 6 + rounded-up text + 6 + badge + 2 — equals the cell's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"fittingSize.width","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":": 77/77 for ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"feature","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", 126/126 for ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rc-git-highlight","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" at medium. It measures the regular weight; an emphasized ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"master","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" fits at 78.5 against 76. Only the ref list emphasizes, and only the tree sizes itself by ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"contentWidth","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"A ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".sourceList","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" outline starts a level-0 cell at x = 25 (the 10 pt row inset plus the disclosure triangle), one ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"indentationPerLevel","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" further per level (14 pt when measured; the tree now sets ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Style.folderIndent","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", 12). Once the column fills the list, it keeps 16 pt between the cell's trailing edge and the list's. AppKit publishes neither. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"TreeViewController.cellTrailingInset","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" records the 16; ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"reportContentWidth","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" reads each cell's start from ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"frameOfCell(atColumn:row:)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" rather than hard-coding 25.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
